{"type":"message","id":"ba969ff1","parentId":"5a7801f8","timestamp":"2026-04-07T14:53:02.257Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_2szfeyxij2g4_1","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"这份图片中的题目内容提取如下：\n\n**主题三 寻访特色民俗**\n\n**(5) 在与藏族同胞交往中，发现藏民早晚将双手藏于藏袍袖中，中午脱下一只或两只袖子，系于腰间，该独特的穿衣方式与当地气候的关系是\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_。**\n\n**(6) 在当地特色民居\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_（填民居名称）住宿时，发现其多用石块砌成，窗小墙厚，门低矮。**"}],"details":{"model":"minimax/MiniMax-VL-01","image":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/6dd42e6d-c7a3-486c-9736-74dff784a7ba.jpg","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775573582223}}
{"type":"message","id":"fcd3a3bc","parentId":"ba969ff1","timestamp":"2026-04-07T14:53:20.610Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a geography question about Tibetan customs and housing. The user said question 6 is a mistake/wrong answer problem. This is about traditional Tibetan dwellings - they are made of stone blocks with small windows, thick walls, and low doors. These features are related to the local climate (cold, high altitude).\n\nThis doesn't look like physics - it's geography about Tibetan customs and architecture. The features (stone walls, small windows, thick walls, low doors) are adaptations to the cold, windy, high-altitude climate of the Tibetan Plateau.\n\nLet me help the user record this in the mistake notebook (错题本). I should ask which subject and what the correct answer should be, or help them record it as a geography mistake.\n\nActually, looking at the context - this seems to be a geography exercise about \"寻访特色民俗\" (visiting special folk customs), specifically about Tibetan customs and dwellings. The features described (stone walls, small windows, thick walls, low doors) are climate adaptations.\n\nLet me help the user record this as a geography mistake in the Feishu bitable. The app_token for the mistake notebook is TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1.\n\nBut wait - the image shows this is question 5 and 6 of a geography exercise. The user says question 6 is the mistake. Question 6 is about Tibetan dwellings (碉房/民居).\n\nLet me help them record this in the mistake notebook. I should:\n1. Identify it's a geography question about Tibetan housing and climate adaptation\n2. Help them record it properly\n\nBut first, I need to understand what the user wants me to do. They sent this with \"6道题为错题\" - does that mean they have 6 questions total that are mistakes? Or just question 6?\n\nLooking at the image again, it shows question 5 and 6. The user said \"(6)题为错题\" meaning question 6 is a mistake.\n\n\nI should clarify whether they want me to record just this one question or if there are additional mistakes they need help with.","thinkingSignature":"56fba3ab0aee73233ad8018df02a472b89806f98451173ad469c3e5d86f2ac21"},{"type":"text","text":"这张是地理题，关于**藏族民居与气候适应**。\n\n**(6)题** — 藏族民居多用石块砌成，窗小墙厚、门低矮，这是因为当地（高原气候，昼夜温差大、风大）需要保暖防风。\n\n**问题**：你有6道错题要记录，还是只有这1道？图片里只看到5和6两道题。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":104542,"output":514,"cacheRead":40516,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":145572,"cost":{"input":0.0313626,"output":0.0006167999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00243096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03441036}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775573582259,"responseId":"06244d4e663063af6ff21928ddd822ee"}}
